content:
  Core technology: DeepCode AI engine (acquired end of 2020).
  Training: ML system trained on millions of open-source code commits.
  Representation: Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) + Event Graph (EG).
    EG enables data-flow-sensitive, context-aware analysis.
  Method: combination of symbolic AI + neural networks.
  Symbolic AI: understands data flow patterns, taint propagation, code semantics.
  Neural networks: pattern matching against learned vulnerability models.
  Scan unit: parses file → analyzes data flow between variables/functions → 
    compares against vulnerability models.
  Interprocedural: tracks tainted data across function boundaries and files.
  Scan speed: typically under 1 minute for most repositories.
  Not purely regex/pattern-based; semantic understanding of taint propagation.
  Contextual dataflow improvement (2024 post): "Analyze Taint Analysis Faster with 
    Improved Contextual Dataflow in Snyk Code"
