keywords: SonarQube, false positive, taint analysis, symbolic execution, dataflow, interprocedural, <5%, injection vulnerability
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  False positive rate (reviewed issues): 3.2% — lower than Google Tricorder's ~5%.
  Analysis techniques combined:
    Taint analysis: dataflow across all files and functions.
    Symbolic execution: simulates real program flows without running program.
    Combination detects problems "only when they are realistically possible."
  Integration: GitHub, Bitbucket Cloud, GitLab, Azure DevOps.
  PR decoration: automated scanning of branches and pull requests.
  Quality gate: go/no-go failing pipelines when code doesn't meet requirements.
  Taint vulnerability presentation: documented at
    https://docs.sonarsource.com/sonarqube-for-vs-code/using/taint-vulnerabilities
    (VS Code extension shows injection vulnerabilities with flow path)
  User workflow: mark findings as accepted false positives with documented rationale.
    Rationale feeds back into rule improvement.
  IDE integration: taint vulnerabilities shown in VS Code, IntelliJ, Visual Studio extensions.
