cites:
cited_by:
content:
  Core challenge addressed: limited context windows + hallucinations degrade bug reports;
    large-scale repo analysis incurs substantial time and token costs.
  Architecture:
    Agent memory: explores codebase on-demand rather than loading whole repo.
    Analyzes dataflow facts along feasible program paths within individual functions.
    Targeted exploration: follows dataflow chains on demand.
  Validator module:
    Verifies data-flow facts for hallucination mitigation.
    Checks satisfiability of path conditions associated with potential bugs.
    Reduces false positives by rejecting infeasible-path findings.
  Results:
    40 true bugs detected across 15 benchmark projects.
    Precision: 78.43%.
    Cost: 0.44 hours and $2.54 per project on average.
    185 new bugs discovered in high-profile projects; 174 confirmed or fixed.
  No specific comparison against static analysis baselines reported in abstract.
<<<END>>>

