id: 17
ts: 2026-05-29T00:16:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Reducing False Positives in Static Bug Detection with LLMs: Industry Empirical Study (Tencent)
authors: (arXiv 2601.18844)
year: 2026
venue: arXiv preprint
quality: PREPRINT
url: https://arxiv.org/html/2601.18844v1
keywords: false positive reduction, LLM, static analysis, industry, Tencent, enterprise, null dereference, use-after-free, buffer overflow, hybrid
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  Context: Tencent's enterprise-customized SAT on Advertising and Marketing Services software.
  Dataset: 433 real alarms (328 false positives, 105 true positives) — FP rate ~75.7% in production.
  Bug types: 3 common categories (null dereference, use-after-free, buffer overflow implied).
  Manual inspection cost: 10-20 minutes per alarm (current workflow).
  Hybrid LLM+SA results:
    Eliminate 94-98% of false positives with strong recall.
    Cost: 2.1-109.5 seconds per alarm (vs. 10-20 min manual).
    Cost: $0.0011-$0.12 per alarm (substantially cheaper than human review).
  First comprehensive empirical study of LLM-based FP reduction in industrial context.
  Key finding: hybrid LLM+SA techniques outperform LLM-only methods.
  Limitation: benchmarks from open-source datasets may not reflect enterprise reality.
<<<END>>>

