SOURCE
id: 19
ts: 2026-05-29T00:17:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: CodeQL SARIF v2.1.0 Output Format — Full Schema
authors: GitHub team
year: 2024
venue: docs.github.com (official documentation)
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/codeql-cli/using-the-advanced-functionality-of-the-codeql-cli/sarif-output
keywords: SARIF, CodeQL, path alert, codeFlows, threadFlows, relatedLocations, physicalLocation, region, severity, ruleId, fingerprint
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  SARIF version: v2.1.0.csd1
  Result fields:
    ruleId: rule identifier (format: language/rule-name)
    ruleIndex: position in rules array
    message: problem description (may use SARIF placeholder syntax)
    locations: single-element array with primary location
    partialFingerprints: dict including primaryLocationLineHash
  Location hierarchy: location → physicalLocation → region
    physicalLocation contains: artifactLocation (always) + optional region/contextRegion
    region formats:
      Line/column: startLine (required), startColumn, endLine, endColumn, snippet
      Character offsets: charOffset, charLength, snippet (when line/col unavailable)
  Path problem output (for @kind path-problem queries):
    results include codeFlows array:
      codeFlow → threadFlows → threadFlowLocation → location
      Each threadFlowLocation has location with optional message.
  relatedLocations: populates when queries use message placeholder options.
    Source and sink of path alerts added to relatedLocations if not in primary location.
    Path alerts show on PRs if source or sink is added/modified.
  Result grouping: default groups by unique message format + primary location.
    --ungroup-results disables grouping.
  Severity: level property set according to @severity in query metadata.
  Rule metadata (reportingDescriptor):
    id, name: rule identifier
    shortDescription: @name property
    fullDescription: @description property
    defaultConfiguration: enabled status and severity level from @severity
  Artifacts: always contain location and index; optional contents with --sarif-add-file-contents.
  Backwards compatibility: always-generated fields never removed; new optional fields may appear.
<<<END>>>

